Hadoop Installation and Running Java MapReduce Program
1. Install Required Software
Install SSH and Java (OpenJDK):
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ssh
sudo apt install pdsh
sudo apt install openjdk-11-jdk
Check Java installation:
java -version
Check Java folder:
ls /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64/
2. Configure Passwordless SSH
Generate SSH key:
ssh-keygen -t rsa -P ""
Add key to authorized users:
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
Test SSH:
ssh localhost
Exit:
exit
3. Extract Hadoop
Extract the Hadoop tar file:
tar -xvzf hadoop-3.*.tar.gz
Rename folder:
mv hadoop-3.* hadoop
Check:
ls
4. Set Environment Variables
Open .bashrc:
nano ~/.bashrc
Add at bottom:
export PDSH_RCMD_TYPE=ssh
export HADOOP_HOME=/home/pict/hadoop
export PATH=$PATH:$HADOOP_HOME/bin
export PATH=$PATH:$HADOOP_HOME/sbin
export HADOOP_MAPRED_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export HADOOP_COMMON_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export HADOOP_HDFS_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export YARN_HOME=$HADOOP_HOME
export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk-amd64
Reload:
source ~/.bashrc
5. Configure Hadoop Files
Go to config folder:
cd ~/hadoop/etc/hadoop
Edit core-site.xml
nano core-site.xml
Add:
<property>
<name>fs.defaultFS</name>
<value>hdfs://localhost:9000</value>
</property>
Edit hdfs-site.xml
nano hdfs-site.xml
Add:
<property>
<name>dfs.replication</name>
<value>1</value>
</property>
<property>
<name>dfs.namenode.name.dir</name>
<value>file:///home/pict/hadoopdata/hdfs/namenode</value>
</property>
<property>
<name>dfs.datanode.data.dir</name>
<value>file:///home/pict/hadoopdata/hdfs/datanode</value>
</property>
6. Create HDFS Directories
mkdir -p ~/hadoopdata/hdfs/namenode
mkdir -p ~/hadoopdata/hdfs/datanode
7. Format NameNode
hdfs namenode -format
8. Start Hadoop
cd ~/hadoop
sbin/start-dfs.sh
Check running processes:
jps
Expected output:
NameNode
DataNode
SecondaryNameNode
Jps
Start YARN:
sbin/start-yarn.sh
Check again:
jps
Expected:
NameNode
DataNode
SecondaryNameNode
ResourceManager
NodeManager
Jps
9. Create Input Directory in HDFS
hdfs dfs -mkdir /input
10. Put Input File in HDFS
Create a sample file:
nano sample.txt
Example text:
hello hadoop
hello world
big data hadoop
Upload to HDFS:
hdfs dfs -put sample.txt /input
Check file:
hdfs dfs -ls /input
11. Compile Java MapReduce Program
Assume your program is WordCount.java
Compile using Hadoop classpath:
javac -classpath $(hadoop classpath) -d wordcount_classes WordCount.java
12. Create JAR File
jar -cvf wordcount.jar -C wordcount_classes/ .
13. Run Java MapReduce Program
hadoop jar wordcount.jar WordCount /input /output
14. Check Output
hdfs dfs -ls /output
Display result:
hdfs dfs -cat /output/part-r-00000
Example output:
big 1
data 1
hadoop 2
hello 2
world 1
15. Stop Hadoop
stop-dfs.sh
stop-yarn.sh
/*
* WordCount MapReduce Program
* ---------------------------------------------------------
* This program counts the number of occurrences of each word
* in a given input file using the MapReduce programming model
* provided by Apache Hadoop.
*
* Steps performed:
* 1. Mapper reads input text line by line.
* 2. Mapper splits each line into words.
* 3. Mapper emits (word, 1).
* 4. Hadoop groups identical keys (Shuffle & Sort phase).
* 5. Reducer sums the values for each word.
* 6. Final output is written to HDFS.
*/
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.StringTokenizer;
/*
* Hadoop configuration class used to configure the job
*/
import org.apache.hadoop.conf.Configuration;
/*
* Represents file paths in HDFS
*/
import org.apache.hadoop.fs.Path;
/*
* Hadoop writable datatypes
* (used instead of normal Java String and int)
*/
import org.apache.hadoop.io.IntWritable;
import org.apache.hadoop.io.Text;
/*
* Core MapReduce classes
*/
import org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.Job;
import org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.Mapper;
import org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.Reducer;
/*
* Classes used to define input and output file paths
*/
import org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.lib.input.FileInputFormat;
import org.apache.hadoop.mapreduce.lib.output.FileOutputFormat;
/*
* Main class that contains Mapper, Reducer and Driver code
*/
public class WordCount {
/*
* -------------------------
* MAPPER CLASS
* -------------------------
*
* Input Key: Object (byte offset of line in file)
* Input Value: Text (one line of text)
*
* Output Key: Text (word)
* Output Value: IntWritable (count = 1)
*/
public static class TokenizerMapper
extends Mapper<Object, Text, Text, IntWritable>{
// Constant value representing one occurrence of a word
private final static IntWritable one = new IntWritable(1);
// Hadoop Text object used to store each word
private Text word = new Text();
/*
* map() method processes one line at a time
*/
public void map(Object key, Text value, Context context)
throws IOException, InterruptedException {
/*
* Convert the line into string and split it into words
* using StringTokenizer
*/
StringTokenizer itr = new StringTokenizer(value.toString());
/*
* Iterate through all tokens (words)
*/
while (itr.hasMoreTokens()) {
// Store the current word
word.set(itr.nextToken());
/*
* Emit key-value pair:
* (word,1)
*/
context.write(word, one);
}
}
}
/*
* -------------------------
* REDUCER CLASS
* -------------------------
*
* Input Key: Text (word)
* Input Value: List of IntWritable values
*
* Output Key: Text (word)
* Output Value: IntWritable (total count)
*/
public static class IntSumReducer
extends Reducer<Text,IntWritable,Text,IntWritable> {
// Variable to store final sum
private IntWritable result = new IntWritable();
/*
* reduce() method aggregates values for each key
*/
public void reduce(Text key, Iterable<IntWritable> values,
Context context)
throws IOException, InterruptedException {
int sum = 0;
/*
* Loop through all values associated with a word
*/
for (IntWritable val : values) {
// Add each value to total
sum += val.get();
}
/*
* Store final count
*/
result.set(sum);
/*
* Emit final output:
* (word,total_count)
*/
context.write(key, result);
}
}
/*
* -------------------------
* DRIVER / MAIN CLASS
* -------------------------
*
* This part configures and launches the MapReduce job.
*/
public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
/*
* Create Hadoop configuration object
*/
Configuration conf = new Configuration();
/*
* Create MapReduce job instance
*/
Job job = Job.getInstance(conf, "word count");
/*
* Specify the jar class containing the program
*/
job.setJarByClass(WordCount.class);
/*
* Set Mapper and Reducer classes
*/
job.setMapperClass(TokenizerMapper.class);
job.setReducerClass(IntSumReducer.class);
/*
* Define output key and value data types
*/
job.setOutputKeyClass(Text.class);
job.setOutputValueClass(IntWritable.class);
/*
* Set input path in HDFS
* args[0] is the input directory
*/
FileInputFormat.addInputPath(job, new Path(args[0]));
/*
* Set output path in HDFS
* args[1] is the output directory
*/
FileOutputFormat.setOutputPath(job, new Path(args[1]));
/*
* Submit job to Hadoop cluster
* Program exits with status 0 if successful
*/
System.exit(job.waitForCompletion(true) ? 0 : 1);
}
}
